│  Final Answer:                                                                                                │
│  **Madrid Travel Guide: A Curated Experience for Art, History, Food, and Culture (Feb 14–16, 2026)**          │
│                                                                                                               │
│  ---                                                                                                          │
│                                                                                                               │
│  ### **Weather & Packing Tips**                                                                               │
│  - **Forecast:** Mild winter with daytime highs of 12°C (45°F) and nighttime lows of 4°C (39°F). Pack         │
│  layers, waterproofs, and a scarf.                                                                            │
│  - **Best Time to Explore:** February is ideal for indoor attractions like museums and historical sites,      │
│  avoiding the summer heat.                                                                                    │
│                                                                                                               │
│  ---                                                                                                          │
│                                                                                                               │
│  ### **Must-Visit Attractions**                                                                               │
│  1. **Prado Museum**                                                                                          │
│     - **Why Visit:** Home to Velázquez’s *Las Meninas*, Goya’s *The Third of May 1808*, and Spain’s greatest  │
│  art collection.                                                                                              │
│     - **Pro Tip:** Skip the crowd by arriving at 9 AM. Explore the **Goya Wing** for lesser-known works.      │
│                                                                                                               │
│  2. **Royal Palace of Madrid**                                                                                │
│     - **Hidden Gem:** The **Palace of Buen Retiro** (free entry) offers serene gardens and the **Royal        │
│  Stables**, a rare glimpse into royal equine history.                                                         │
│                                                                                                               │
│  3. **Reina Sofía Museum**                                                                                    │
│     - **Cultural Spotlight:** Must-see *Guernica* by Picasso. Don’t miss the **Sala de los Austrias** for     │
│  Diego Velázquez’s *Las Meninas* (a smaller version).                                                         │
│                                                                                                               │
│  4. **Thyssen-Bornemisza Museum**                                                                             │
│     - **Diverse Collection:** A “one-stop shop” for art spanning 500 years, from Rembrandt to contemporary    │
│  works.                                                                                                       │
│                                                                                                               │
│  5. **Plaza Mayor**                                                                                           │
│     - **Local Secret:** Stroll the 17th-century square at sunset. Grab a *café con leche* at **Café Gijón**,  │
│  a historic spot frequented by locals.                                                                        │
│                                                                                                               │
│  ---                                                                                                          │
│                                                                                                               │
│  ### **Hidden Gems & Local Favorites**                                                                        │
│  - **Casa de las Flores (Carmen Conde Museum):** A 17th-century mansion with private art collections and a    │
│  hidden courtyard garden.                                                                                     │
│  - **Parque del Retiro:** A peaceful escape with the **Fontaine de la Ciutat** and the **Palacio de           │
│  Cristal** (a glasshouse with panoramic views).                                                               │
│  - **Museo Sorolla:** A lesser-known gem showcasing modernist painter Joaquín Sorolla’s sunlit landscapes.    │
│                                                                                                               │
│  ---                                                                                                          │
│                                                                                                               │
│  ### **Food & Drink: A Culinary Journey**                                                                     │
│  - **La Latina:**                                                                                             │
│    - **Must-Try:** *Cocido madrileño* (slow-cooked stew) at **Casa Miguel** or *tortilla española* (Spanish   │
│  omelet) at **Casa de la Infanta**.                                                                           │
│    - **Local Tip:** Visit **Mercado de San Miguel** for tapas and flamenco shows.                             │
│  - **Chueca District:**                                                                                       │
│    - **Gay-Friendly Vibes:** Try *churros con chocolate* at **Café de Chinita** and explore the **Casa de     │
│  Velázquez** for art-themed dining.                                                                           │
│  - **Street Food:** Grab *pan con tomate* (tomato bread) and *empanadas* from street vendors in **Santander   │
│  Street**.                                                                                                    │
│                                                                                                               │
│  ---                                                                                                          │
│                                                                                                               │
│  ### **Special Events (Feb 2026)**                                                                            │
│  - **Madrid Art Fair (Feria de Arte de Madrid):** Held in February, this event showcases emerging and         │
│  established Spanish artists.                                                                                 │
│  - **Winter Festivals:** Look for **Feria de San Isidro** (late February) for traditional folk music and      │
│  crafts.                                                                                                      │
│                                                                                                               │
│  ---                                                                                                          │
│                                                                                                               │
│  ### **Practical Tips**                                                                                       │
│  - **Transport:** Use the **Madrid Metro** (€1.50 per ride) or the **Madrid Pass** (€25 for 10 rides).        │
│  Walkable areas: Centro, Malasaña, and Retiro.                                                                │
│  - **Accommodation:** Book centrally located hotels in **Centro** (€100–€150/night) or budget-friendly        │
│  **Chueca** hostels (€40–€70/night).                                                                          │
│  - **Budgeting:** Entry to museums is €12–€15; meals average €10–€15. Avoid tourist traps by using apps like  │
│  **TripAdvisor** or **Google Maps**.                                                                          │
│                                                                                                               │
│  ---                                                                                                          │
│                                                                                                               │
│  ### **Why Madrid > Dubai**                                                                                   │
│  - **Cultural Depth:** Madrid’s art and history are unmatched—Dubai’s attractions cater to modern             │
│  experiences.                                                                                                 │
│  - **Cost-Effective:** Flights from Vienna to Madrid start at €30 (Skyscanner), vs. Dubai’s steep costs.      │
│  - **Weather:** February in Madrid is mild, while Dubai’s humidity and heat can deter exploration of          │
│  historical sites.                                                                                            │
